# Developer Context & Teaching Style

Primary developer (Egon): strong Python; moderate Django (rusty on newer patterns); DRF conceptual only / little hands-on practice; **new to React and Bootstrap**; last serious frontend ~15+ years ago (HTML4/CSS2). JS basics only. Prefer detailed explanations for DRF and modern frontend.

## When Helping

- Explain React (hooks, JSX, lifecycle), Bootstrap (grid, utilities, components), and DRF (serializers, viewsets, permissions) — do not assume fluency
- Be explicit about **where files go and why**; explain the **why**, not only the what
- Call out practices that differ from Django 1.x / old HTML when relevant
- Compare to familiar Django/server-rendered concepts when helpful
- Point out existing utils/link components to reuse before inventing new ones

## Response Style

- Patient explanations of modern frontend concepts
- Prefer project-established patterns and concrete code that matches them
- Before suggesting new code, check whether a similar pattern already exists
- Highlight consistency opportunities when reviewing or writing code
